300 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 91 0 R
/T (A Python variable is just a name that refers to an object; it has no fixed type. x = 10 makes x an int, and x = 'ten' later makes it a str \(shown in the output\). Multiple assignment a, b = 4.2, 8.7 assigns both in one statement, and a, b = b, a swaps them without a temporary variable, because the right side is fully evaluated first.)
/E (A Python variable is just a name that refers to an object; it has no fixed type. x = 10 makes x an int, and x = 'ten' later makes it a str \(shown in the output\). Multiple assignment a, b = 4.2, 8.7 assigns both in one statement, and a, b = b, a swaps them without a temporary variable, because the right side is fully evaluated first.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [17]
>>
