616 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 96 0 R
/T (1. Import forms: import milkrate loads the module and you use names as milkrate.payout\(...\), so there is no clash with your own names. from milkrate import payout copies only the name payout into your namespace so you call payout\(...\) directly \(shorter, but could shadow another payout\). import milkrate as mr imports the whole module under a short alias, mr.payout\(...\).)
/E (1. Import forms: import milkrate loads the module and you use names as milkrate.payout\(...\), so there is no clash with your own names. from milkrate import payout copies only the name payout into your namespace so you call payout\(...\) directly \(shorter, but could shadow another payout\). import milkrate as mr imports the whole module under a short alias, mr.payout\(...\).)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
617 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 96 0 R
/T (2. if __name__ == '__main__': when a file is run directly Python sets __name__ to '__main__'; when it is imported __name__ is the module name \('milkrate'\). The test therefore runs the demonstration only when the file is executed directly. 3. Without that guard the demonstration table would be printed \(and any other top-level actions would run\) every)
/E (2. if __name__ == '__main__': when a file is run directly Python sets __name__ to '__main__'; when it is imported __name__ is the module name \('milkrate'\). The test therefore runs the demonstration only when the file is executed directly. 3. Without that guard the demonstration table would be printed \(and any other top-level actions would run\) every)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
