697 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 97 0 R
/T (Maintainability/rate revision: with a module, a rate revision is made in one file \(one place\) and every script gets it; with copies the same edit must be repeated in every script and a missed copy gives different payments for the same milk. One-time cost of importing: the first import finds, compiles \(to .pyc\) and executes the module once; this costs a little time \(typically fractions of a millisecond to a few milliseconds\) but happens only once per program run. sys.modules: Python keeps a dictionary of every imported module. After the first import the module object is stored in sys.modules \(the output shows 'milkrate in sys.modules: True'\); any later 'import milkrate' just returns the stored object without reading or running the file again, so repeated imports are almost free.)
/E (Maintainability/rate revision: with a module, a rate revision is made in one file \(one place\) and every script gets it; with copies the same edit must be repeated in every script and a missed copy gives different payments for the same milk. One-time cost of importing: the first import finds, compiles \(to .pyc\) and executes the module once; this costs a little time \(typically fractions of a millisecond to a few milliseconds\) but happens only once per program run. sys.modules: Python keeps a dictionary of every imported module. After the first import the module object is stored in sys.modules \(the output shows 'milkrate in sys.modules: True'\); any later 'import milkrate' just returns the stored object without reading or running the file again, so repeated imports are almost free.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
