1057 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 101 0 R
/T (A farmer can only be paid a whole number of paise, so the bank really transfers the sum of the individually rounded payments. Rounding only the final total gives a different number \(about Rs 19.58 less for 150,000 payments in this experiment\), which would not match what was actually paid to the farmers. Therefore round every payment to 2 decimals \(preferably with Decimal\) and add the rounded values. \(The test payments here are synthetic, with 4 decimal places before rounding; the point - rounding position changes the total - holds for real data.\))
/E (A farmer can only be paid a whole number of paise, so the bank really transfers the sum of the individually rounded payments. Rounding only the final total gives a different number \(about Rs 19.58 less for 150,000 payments in this experiment\), which would not match what was actually paid to the farmers. Therefore round every payment to 2 decimals \(preferably with Decimal\) and add the rounded values. \(The test payments here are synthetic, with 4 decimal places before rounding; the point - rounding position changes the total - holds for real data.\))
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [30]
>>
endobj
