1276 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 105 0 R
/T (Decision: modify the original design \(keep module + functions + named constants + validation + tests; change the number type to Decimal, replace the single rate constants by rate cards chosen by month, drop whole-step rounding, add a bonus function\). Tests T1-T11 above include the original rates \(T1, T6, T9, T10\), the seasonal rates \(T2-T5\), April as the first seasonal month \(T5\), July as the first normal month \(T6\), and with/without bonus \(T7-T10, including exactly 500 L giving no bonus because the rule says more than 500\). All 11 passed, so the revised design meets the new requirements. Trade-offs: Decimal is slower than float \(about 2.5 microseconds per entry, Task 11\) but exact; rate cards add a parameter to every function but make seasonal changes a data change; proportional steps change prices slightly compared with the old rule \(table in B\) but follow the stated rate \(Rs 0.40 per 0.1% means Rs 0.04 per 0.01%\). Assumptions: the bonus applies to all litres of the ten days \(not only the litres above 500\) when the total is more than 500; the season is decided by one month number for the whole ten-day period \(a period that crosses 31 March/30 June is not handled\); the rate is rounded to paise before multiplying by litres \(e.g. 3.77/8.63 in May gives 33.605 -> 33.61, payment 336.10\); the SNF range 7.0-10.0 is assumed. If the co-operative decides differently on any of these, only the named constants/one function need to change.)
/E (Decision: modify the original design \(keep module + functions + named constants + validation + tests; change the number type to Decimal, replace the single rate constants by rate cards chosen by month, drop whole-step rounding, add a bonus function\). Tests T1-T11 above include the original rates \(T1, T6, T9, T10\), the seasonal rates \(T2-T5\), April as the first seasonal month \(T5\), July as the first normal month \(T6\), and with/without bonus \(T7-T10, including exactly 500 L giving no bonus because the rule says more than 500\). All 11 passed, so the revised design meets the new requirements. Trade-offs: Decimal is slower than float \(about 2.5 microseconds per entry, Task 11\) but exact; rate cards add a parameter to every function but make seasonal changes a data change; proportional steps change prices slightly compared with the old rule \(table in B\) but follow the stated rate \(Rs 0.40 per 0.1% means Rs 0.04 per 0.01%\). Assumptions: the bonus applies to all litres of the ten days \(not only the litres above 500\) when the total is more than 500; the season is decided by one month number for the whole ten-day period \(a period that crosses 31 March/30 June is not handled\); the rate is rounded to paise before multiplying by litres \(e.g. 3.77/8.63 in May gives 33.605 -> 33.61, payment 336.10\); the SNF range 7.0-10.0 is assumed. If the co-operative decides differently on any of these, only the named constants/one function need to change.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
