1707 0 obj
<<
/Title (1. What changed: \(i\) the analyser gives fat and SNF with two decimal places \(e.g. 3.77%\), so readings are finer than the 0.1% step; \(ii\) from April to June the base rate is Rs 32.00 and each fat step is worth Rs 0.45 \(SNF step unchanged at 0.30\); \(iii\) a farmer supplying more than 500 litres in ten days receives a bonus of Rs 0.50 per litre.)
/Dest [25 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1572 0 R
/Next 1833 0 R
>>
endobj
1708 0 obj
<<
/Title (3. Effect of two-decimal readings on steps and rounding: step counts become fractional \(0.27 / 0.1 = 2.7\). If the old nearest-whole-step rule is kept, nearby readings get the same price and prices are off by up to half a step \(Rs 0.20/litre for fat\), and exact ties \(x.5 steps\) arise. Float arithmetic also makes these fractional steps inexact, so Decimal is needed. Rates such as 33.605 need an explicit rounding rule \(half up, to paise\).)
/Dest [25 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1572 0 R
/Prev 1833 0 R
>>
endobj
